name: clamp-is-elementwise-min-max
why: The clamp idiom min(max(x, lo), hi) is ELEMENTWISE — min/max compare their arguments within one record and never look back at earlier samples (the windowed forms are rollingMin/rollingMax(x, N), M28.3). 1 clamps up to 2, 3 stays, 5 clamps down to 4.
expr: min(max(nodeA.price, 2), 4)
keys: nodeA.price
resolve: STRICT
--- LOG ---
---
#00:00:01.000 [t] INFO L
eventLogRecord:
  logTime: 1
  event: E
  nodeLogs:
    - nodeA: { price: 1.0}
---
#00:00:02.000 [t] INFO L
eventLogRecord:
  logTime: 2
  event: E
  nodeLogs:
    - nodeA: { price: 3.0}
---
#00:00:03.000 [t] INFO L
eventLogRecord:
  logTime: 3
  event: E
  nodeLogs:
    - nodeA: { price: 5.0}
--- EXPECT ---
1 => 2.0
2 => 3.0
3 => 4.0
